<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n68218" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μνῆστις</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		 and 
			Aeol.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μνᾶστ-</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιος</span>, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>remembrance, recollection, heed</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδέ τις ἡμῖν δόρπου μνῆστις ἔην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					13.280
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔστι παρέντων μνᾶστιν ἐπιθέσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alcm.
					64
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλλ᾽ ἴσχε κἀμοῦ μ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					520
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				1269
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅτου . . ἀπορρεῖ μ.</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				523
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μνᾶστίν τινος παρέχειν τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					28.23
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὕτω δὴ Γέλωνος μνῆστις
			γέγονε</span> then you bethought yourselves of Gelon, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.158
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>memory, fame</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Simon.
				4.3
			</span></i>.</div>
